A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at 1Ch.9.14; 
only referred to as Hashabiah (חֲשַׁבְיָ֫הוּ); 
a son of Bunni; 
father of Azrikam.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.25.3; 
only referred to as Hashabiah (חֲשַׁבְיָ֫הוּ); 
son of Jeduthun; 
a brother of Obed-edom, Mattithiah, Gedaliah, Zeri, Jeshaiah.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at 1Ch.9.14; 
only referred to as Hasshub (חַשּׁוּב); 
a son of Azrikam; 
father of Shemaiah.

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.3.20; 
only referred to as Hashubah (חֲשֻׁבָה); 
son of Zerubbabel; 
a brother of Meshullam, Hananiah, Shelomith, Ohel, Berechiah, Hasadiah, Jushab-hesed, Abiud. § a son of Zerubbabel

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.6.45; 
only referred to as Hashabiah (חֲשַׁבְיָ֫הוּ); 
a son of Amaziah; 
father of Malluch.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.27.17; 
only referred to as Hashabiah (חֲשַׁבְיָ֫הוּ); 
a son of Kemuel.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.11.22; 
only referred to as Hashabiah (חֲשַׁבְיָ֫הוּ); 
son of Mattaniah; 
a brother of Shemaiah; 
father of Bani.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.3.10; 
only referred to as Hashabneiah (חֲשַׁבְנְיָה); 
father of Hattush.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.3.11; 
only referred to as Hasshub (חַשּׁוּב); 
a son of Pahath-moab.

A man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Num.1.15; 
only referred to as Enan (עֵינָן); 
father of Ahira. § a prince of the tribe of Naphtali at the census at Mount Sinai

A location first mentioned at Jos.17.11; 
only referred to as En-dor (עֵין־דֹּר). § a place in the territory of Issachar yet possessed by Manasseh; located 4 miles (6.5 km) north of Tabor
place of residence of the spiritist consulted by king Saul

A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.11.26; 
only referred to as Haran (הָרָן); 
son of Terah; 
a brother of Abraham, Nahor and Sarah; 
father of Lot, Milcah and Iscah.

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.4.8; 
only referred to as Harum (הָרֻם); 
son of Koz; 
a brother of Anub and Zobebah; 
father of Aharhel. § a man of Judah, father of Aharhel

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.23.9;
only referred to as Haran (הָרָן); 
son of Shimei; 
a brother of Zimmah, Shelomoth and Haziel.

A man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Num.1.14; 
referred to as Deuel (דְּעוּאֵל), or Reuel (רְעוּאֵל); 
father of Eliasaph. § father of Eliasaph, the captain of the tribe of Gad at the time of the numbering of the people at Sinai, also called 'Reuel'

A priest from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at 1Ch.9.10; 
only referred to as Jedaiah (יְדַעְיָה); 
a son of Joiarib.

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at 1Ch.7.6; 
only referred to as Jediael (יְדִיעֲאֵל); 
son of Benjamin; 
a brother of Bela, Becher, Ashbel, Gera, Naaman, Ahiram, Rosh, Muppim, Huppim, Ard and Ahiram; 
father of Bilhan.

A High Priest from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at Neh.12.11; 
only referred to as Jaddua (יַדּוּעַ); 
a son of Johanan.

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.2.28; 
only referred to as Jada (יָדָע); 
son of Onam; 
a brother of Shammai; 
father of Jether and Jonathan. § a Judahite, son of Onam and brother of Shammai, in the genealogy of the sons of Jerahmeel by his wife Atarah

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.11.45; 
only referred to as Jediael (יְדִיעֲאֵל); 
son of Shimri; 
a brother of Joha.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.26.2; 
only referred to as Jediael (יְדִיעֲאֵל); 
son of Meshelemiah; 
a brother of Zechariah, Zebadiah, Jathniel, Elam, Jehohanan and Eliehoenai.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.6.20; 
only referred to as Zimmah (זִמָּה); 
son of Shimei; 
father of Joah; 
a brother of Shelomoth, Haziel, and Haran.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2Ch.29.12; 
only referred to as Zimmah (זִמָּה); 
father of Joah.

A woman living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.15.33; 
referred to as Jerusha or Jerushah (NIV= Jerusha) (יְרוּשָׁא, יְרוּשָׁה); 
a daughter of Zadok; 
wife of Uzziah; 
mother of Jotham. § the wife of king Uzziah and mother of king Jotham of Judah

witness, testimony; martyr (one who witnessed unto death) 
(1) a judicial witness, deponent, testimony Mt. 18:16; Heb. 10:28; 
(2) generally, a witness to a circumstance, Lk. 24:48; Acts 10:41; in NT a witness, a testifier, of a doctrine, Rev. 1:5; 3:14; 11:3; 
(3) a martyr, Acts 22:20; Rev. 2:13

to credit, count, reckon; regard, think, consider 
(1) primarily to count, calculate; to count, enumerate, consider Mk. 15:28; Lk. 22:37; to set down as a matter of account, 1Cor. 13:5; 2Cor. 3:5; 12:6; to impute, credit, count, consider, reckon Rom. 4:3; 2Cor. 5:19; 2Tim. 4:16; to account, Rom. 2:26; 8:36; εἰς οὐδὲν λογισθῆναι, to be set at nought, despised, Acts 19:27; to regard, deem, consider, Rom. 6:11; 14:14; 1Cor. 4:1; 2Cor. 10:2; Phil. 3:13; 
(2) to infer, conclude, presume, Rom. 2:3; 3:28; 8:18; 2Cor. 10:2, 7, 11; Heb. 11:19; 1Pet. 5:12; 
(3) to think upon, ponder, Phil. 4:8; absolute to reason, Mk. 11:31; 1Cor. 13:11

A High Priest living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Sa.1.3; 
only referred to as Eli (עֵלִי); 
father of Hophni, Phinehas. § descendant of Aaron through Ithamar and high priest and judge of Israel when Samuel entered service as a child

A location first mentioned at Num.34.4; 
only referred to as Akrabbim (עַקְרַבִּים). § a pass on the southern border of Palestine
scorpion-pass; ascent of Akrabbim

A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.36.23; 
referred to as Alvan or Alvan (עַלְיָן, עַלְוָן); 
son of Shobal; 
a brother of Manahath, Ebal, Shepho and Onam. § a Horite, son of Shobal

A female deity of Sidon in the time of the Old Testament, first mentioned at 1Ki.11.5, also known as Astarte; 
only referred to as Ashtoreth (עַשְׁתֹּ֫רֶת) § the principal female deity of the Phoenicians worshipped in war and fertility
1a) also 'Ishtar' of Assyria and 'Astarte' by the Greeks and Romans

A location first mentioned at Deu.1.4; 
referred to as Ashtaroth (עַשְׁתָּרוֹת), or Beeshterah (NIV= Be Eshterah) (בְּעֶשְׁתְּרָה), or Ashterathite (עַשְׁתְּרָתִי). § Ashterathite, of Astaroth "star"
an inhabitant of the city of Ashtaroth

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at Jer.36.26; 
only referred to as Hammelech (הַמֶּלֶךְ); 
father of Jerahmeel and Malchijah. § A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at Jer.36.26; 
father of: Jerahmeel (H3396I) and Malchijah (H4441H); also translated "the king";

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.2.37; 
only referred to as Ephlal (אֶפְלָל); 
a son of Zabad; 
father of Obed. § a descendant of Pharez

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.3.25; 
only referred to as Palal (פָּלָל); 
a son of Uzai. § son of Uzai and one who assisted in restoring the walls of Jerusalem in the time of Nehemiah

A priest living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.11.12; 
only referred to as Pelaliah (פְּלַלְיָה); 
a son of Amzi; 
father of Jeroham. § son of Amzi and ancestor of Adaiah the priest in the time of Nehemiah

A Singer from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at 1Ch.9.21; 
only referred to as Zechariah (זְכַרְיָהוּ); 
son of Meshelemiah; 
a brother of Jediael, Zebadiah, Jathniel, Elam, Jehohanan and Eliehoenai.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.25.2; 
only referred to as Zaccur (זַכּוּר); 
son of Asaph; 
a brother of Joseph, Nethaniah and Asharelah.

A king of Northern Israel, living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.14.29; 
only referred to as Zechariah (זְכַרְיָהוּ); 
a son of Jeroboam. § 11th in order of the minor prophets; a priest, son of Berechiah and grandson of Iddo, who, along with Haggai, directed the rebuilding of the temple in the days of Zerubbabel

A prophet living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at Ezr.5.1; 
referred to as Zechariah (זְכַרְיָהוּ), or Zechariah (Aramiac זְכַרְיָה); 
a son of Berechiah. § 11th in order of the minor prophets; a priest, son of Berechiah and grandson of Iddo, who, along with Haggai, directed the rebuilding of the temple in the days of Zerubbabel

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.18.2; 
only referred to as Zechariah (זְכַרְיָהוּ); 
father of Abi. § 11th in order of the minor prophets; a priest, son of Berechiah and grandson of Iddo, who, along with Haggai, directed the rebuilding of the temple in the days of Zerubbabel

A man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, only mentioned at Num.13.4; 
only referred to as Zaccur (זַכּוּר); 
father of Shammua.

A man from the tribe of Simeon living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.4.26; 
only referred to as Zaccur (זַכּוּר); 
a son of Hammuel; 
father of Shimei.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.24.27; 
only referred to as Zaccur (זַכּוּר); 
son of Jaaziah; 
a brother of Beno, Shoham and Ibri.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.3.2; 
only referred to as Zaccur (זַכּוּר); 
a son of Imri.

A priest living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.13.13; 
only referred to as Zaccur (זַכּוּר); 
a son of Mattaniah; 
father of Hanan.

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.8.31; 
referred to as Zecher (זֶ֫כֶר), or Zechariah (זְכַרְיָהוּ); 
son of Abiel and Maacah; 
a brother of Kish, Ner, Abdon, Zur, Baal, Nadab, Gedor, Ahio and Mikloth. § a Gibeonite

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, only mentioned at Exo.6.21; 
only referred to as Zichri (זִכְרִי); 
son of Izhar; 
a brother of Korah, Nepheg and Shelomith.

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.8.19; 
only referred to as Zichri (זִכְרִי); 
son of Shimei; 
a brother of Jakim, Zabdi, Elienai, Zillethai, Eliel, Adaiah, Beraiah and Shimrath.

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.8.23; 
only referred to as Zichri (זִכְרִי); 
son of Shashak; 
a brother of Ishpan, Eber, Eliel, Abdon, Hanan, Hananiah, Elam, Anthothijah, Iphdeiah and Penuel.

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.8.27; 
only referred to as Zichri (זִכְרִי); 
son of Jeroham; 
a brother of Shamsherai, Shehariah, Athaliah, Jaareshiah and Elijah.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at 1Ch.9.15; 
referred to as Zichri (זִכְרִי), or Zabdi (זַבְדִּי); 
a son of Asaph; 
father of Mica.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.26.25; 
only referred to as Zichri (זִכְרִי); 
a son of Joram; 
father of Shelomoth.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.27.16; 
only referred to as Zichri (זִכְרִי); 
father of Eliezer.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2Ch.17.16; 
only referred to as Zichri (זִכְרִי); 
father of Amasiah.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2Ch.23.1; 
only referred to as Zichri (זִכְרִי); 
father of Elishaphat.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.11.9; 
only referred to as Zichri (זִכְרִי); 
father of Joel.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.24.25; 
only referred to as Zechariah (זְכַרְיָהוּ); 
a son of Isshiah. § 11th in order of the minor prophets; a priest, son of Berechiah and grandson of Iddo, who, along with Haggai, directed the rebuilding of the temple in the days of Zerubbabel

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.26.11; 
only referred to as Zechariah (זְכַרְיָהוּ); 
son of Hosah; 
a brother of Shimri, Hilkiah and Tebaliah. § 11th in order of the minor prophets; a priest, son of Berechiah and grandson of Iddo, who, along with Haggai, directed the rebuilding of the temple in the days of Zerubbabel

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.27.21; 
only referred to as Zechariah (זְכַרְיָהוּ); 
father of Iddo. § 11th in order of the minor prophets; a priest, son of Berechiah and grandson of Iddo, who, along with Haggai, directed the rebuilding of the temple in the days of Zerubbabel

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2Ch.20.14; 
only referred to as Zechariah (זְכַרְיָהוּ); 
a son of Benaiah; 
father of Jahaziel. § 11th in order of the minor prophets; a priest, son of Berechiah and grandson of Iddo, who, along with Haggai, directed the rebuilding of the temple in the days of Zerubbabel

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2Ch.21.2; 
only referred to as Zechariah (זְכַרְיָהוּ); 
son of Jehoshaphat; 
a brother of Jehoram, Azariah, Jehiel, Azariahu, Michael and Shephatiah. § 11th in order of the minor prophets; a priest, son of Berechiah and grandson of Iddo, who, along with Haggai, directed the rebuilding of the temple in the days of Zerubbabel

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Ezr.8.11; 
only referred to as Zechariah (זְכַרְיָהוּ); 
a son of Bebai. § 11th in order of the minor prophets; a priest, son of Berechiah and grandson of Iddo, who, along with Haggai, directed the rebuilding of the temple in the days of Zerubbabel

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.11.4; 
only referred to as Zechariah (זְכַרְיָהוּ); 
a son of Amariah; 
father of Uzziah. § 11th in order of the minor prophets; a priest, son of Berechiah and grandson of Iddo, who, along with Haggai, directed the rebuilding of the temple in the days of Zerubbabel

